Package: GLAMMGoF
Title: Resampling-Based Predictive Validation for Generalized Linear and Generalized Additive Models
Date: 2026-08-19
URL: https://github.com/colinpshea/glammgof
Version: 1.4.2
Authors@R: 
    person("Colin", "Shea", , "colin.shea@myfwc.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2906-250X"))
Description: Provides resampling-based predictive validation for generalized
    linear and generalized additive models (with or without random effects)
    fitted using packages such as glmmTMB, mgcv, stats, lme4, and MASS.
    Predictive performance is assessed using either repeated random holdout
    (Monte Carlo cross-validation) or bootstrap resampling with out-of-bag
    evaluation. In each replicate, models are refit to a training dataset and
    evaluated on separate test data, generating sampling distributions of
    in-sample and out-of-sample performance statistics. Supported metrics
    include relative root mean squared error, relative mean absolute error,
    relative median absolute error, and relative bias for continuous or
    integer responses, and AUC, Brier score, and log loss for binary
    responses. By default, metrics are based on population-level predictions,
    excluding random effects where present; conditional and bias-adjusted
    predictions are also available. Bias adjustment addresses the
    underestimation of the arithmetic mean that arises from Jensen's
    inequality when back-transforming predictions to the response scale, via
    analytical corrections for log-link and log-normal models, with or without
    random effects. Marginal and bias-adjusted response-scale predictions can
    also be calculated using parametric bootstrapping.
